  "note": "Table 5 measured under one metrics.py. The inner-solver settings differ by method and are recorded in methods[*]: the top-level pcg_max and refine are null because the index is written by whichever process finishes last, which here was the Thomas-Fermi job. All fourteen runs are fp64 with fp32 Krylov vectors in the inner solve (--fp32-inner). The twelve non-Thomas-Fermi runs used the defaults --pcg-max 200 --refine 1 (jobs redo999_a..f); the two Thomas-Fermi runs used the short-burst schedule --pcg-max 25 --refine 6 (job tf999d), without which that metric stalls. Flows carry an fp64 conjugate direction and the CG variants an fp32 one (--cg-dir-fp32). The twelve non-TF entries were reconstructed from the per-process job logs after a concurrent-write race; the CSVs were never at risk."
